 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "status": "todo", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+
+`status` is `todo` (the default), `doing` or `done`. Any other value answers 400 `{ "error": "status must be todo, doing or done" }`.
+
+**`done` is deprecated** and will be removed in the next release; use `status`. For now responses still include `done` (`true` exactly when the status is `done`), `PATCH` (and `POST`) still accept `done: true` (status `done`) and `done: false` (status `todo`), and `?done=true|false` still filters (`false` means `todo` or `doing`). If both `status` and `done` are sent, `status` wins.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?status=todo\|doing\|done` keeps the tasks in that status (deprecated: `?done=true` or `?done=false`) | 200, an array of tasks |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` and optionally `"status"` | 201, the task |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `status` (deprecated: `done`) | 200, the task, or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
 Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
 
 ## Layout
 
-- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
+- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied; the second one replaced the `done` column by `status`).
 - `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
 - `src/app.ts`: the HTTP server and its routes.
 - `public/`: the page.
 - `test/`: the API tests, against a server on a random port with an in-memory database.
